CONTROLLER — agent layer over the existing matching stack
============================================================================================================

  CHANGE 1: fee widening is now PER BATCH, not global.
      OFF for BenchRec eval — real BenchRec has effectively no fee deductions,
      so the widened band admits only false candidates (overall match
      91.794% -> 75.181%) and masks the no_candidate trigger by guaranteeing a
      non-empty pool (1,408 -> 165 firings).
      ON for the synthetic batch — it contains fees by construction (9.4% of
      groups), where widening gained +4.750 points of overall match.
      Both settings are run against both batches below so this is shown.

  CHANGE 2: low_confidence thresholds are FITTED ON TRAIN ONLY.

Ranking BenchRec train and fitting the completion classifier (train only).
  19,339 candidate decisions, 8,905 positive (46.05%), fitted in 110.9s

