  Grid searched against train's inline targetAllocation labels. Eval and the
  synthetic batches are not consulted at any point in this section.

  'lc_fired' counts rows where the trigger fires at all (non-exclusive — the
  framing the 68.7% eval figure used). 'lc_only' counts rows the trigger alone
  removes from auto-close, which is its true marginal cost.

  CAVEAT: the completion classifier's probabilities on train are IN-SAMPLE, so
  completion_added behaves better here than it will out of sample. That shifts
  which rows are already escalated by other triggers, so lc_only is mildly
  optimistic. The score/margin thresholds themselves do not depend on it.

